        "title": "Contemporary Practice: Natural Dye Revival, Slow Fashion, Fiber Arts",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The 21st-century natural dye revival is driven by two overlapping communities: textile artists interested in historical technique and aesthetic quality, and environmental advocates seeking low-impact alternatives to industrial synthetic dyeing. The science has improved (better understanding of lightfastness, mordant safety), the supply chain has developed (specialist dye plant suppliers, online communities), and the slow fashion movement has given natural dyes a cultural context that extends beyond craft practice."
